2. Jump button must ALWAYS use an upward arrow

Current issue

The current mobile presentation system includes Jump among the buttons that display frames of the selected fighter’s animations.

Relevant code:

* js/ui/mobile-abilities.js
* js/game/touch-controls.js
* js/ui/icons.js
* js/data/characters.js

SPRITE_BUTTONS includes jump, and jumpArt() can return a character-specific sprite.

Consequently, the Jump button changes appearance depending on the selected fighter.

Required change

Jump must always display one universal, recognizable upward arrow.

Use the existing ICONS.jump arrow design as the starting point, or refine its SVG for clarity.

The icon must:

* Clearly point upward.
* Remain identical for every fighter.
* Remain identical when grounded, jumping, falling, or attacking.
* Work in both Joystick and Classic mobile layouts.
* Remain readable at every supported control size.
* Preserve its accessible label, Jump.

Technical requirements

1. Remove jump from the fighter-specific sprite-preview workflow.
2. Adjust jumpArt() or replace that presentation path so it always returns the universal SVG without a fighter sprite.
3. Update TouchControls.setCharacter() so selecting a fighter cannot replace the arrow.
4. Remove obsolete mobileAbilities.jump.preview entries from character definitions if they are no longer used.
5. Preserve data-action="jump" and all existing jump input behavior.

Do not change jump physics, variable jump height, air jumps, cooldowns, or any other gameplay behavior.

Expected result

Selecting #0001, #0002, or another fighter never changes the Jump icon. An upward arrow remains visible at all times.

