3. Completely remove the mobile Down arrow button

Current issue

Both mobile control schemes currently expose a Down button.

In js/game/touch-controls.js:

* Classic uses a DPAD entry with action: 'down'.
* Joystick creates STICK_DOWN, an additional Down button beside the stick.

The control also appears in customization data, CSS, tests, and comments.

Required change

Remove the Down arrow button completely from both mobile layouts and their supporting UI definitions.

It must not remain hidden, transparent, or merely disabled. The unused button element and all button-specific code must be removed.

A. Classic Buttons

Change the directional cluster from:

[LEFT] [DOWN] [RIGHT]

To:

[LEFT] [RIGHT]

Adjust spacing and pointer hit-testing to make the two remaining buttons work correctly.

Dragging a finger from Left to Right and back should continue to update directional input normally.

B. Joystick

Remove the Down button positioned beside the joystick.

Keep the joystick and its Left mouvement and Right mouvement Dash buttons.

Recenter or adjust the joystick cluster as necessary to eliminate the unused space.

Keep the joystick’s original horizontal movement behavior.

C. Remove obsolete code

Inspect and clean up:

* DPAD
* STICK_DOWN
* this.stickDown
* Down-related button creation and event listeners
* Down button references in allButtons
* Scheme switching and control-element lookup
* Joystick positioning calculations
* Down-specific touch-control CSS
* Down button entries in TOUCH_CONTROL_IDS
* Touch layout editor registration and selection
* Tests that expect the old button
* Comments or documentation describing the removed button

In styles.css, review definitions such as:

* --tc-down
* --tc-stick-left
* .tc-stick-down

Remove or simplify styling that exists exclusively for the deleted button.

Remove ICONS.down only if it has no remaining legitimate consumers.

D. Existing saved layouts

The touch layout system stores customized positions and scales using stable control IDs.

Old saved layouts may contain down.

Update layout sanitization so obsolete down entries are discarded gracefully.

Preserve every other valid customized control position and size.

Previously saved settings must load without errors, invisible hit targets, or shifted controls.

E. Preserve legitimate Down functionality

This request removes the mobile Down arrow button, not every internal use of the word down.

Preserve gameplay mechanics that still legitimately use the Down input through keyboard, gamepad, or CPU behavior, including fast-fall or launch steering.

Also preserve downward navigation in menus and the layout editor.

Do not blindly delete down from CONFIG.ACTIONS, input snapshots, keyboard bindings, or menu navigation if doing so would break existing gameplay.

Remove the obsolete touch-control UI functionality thoroughly without deleting unrelated mechanics.

Expected result

Neither mobile control scheme nor the customization editor contains a Down arrow button or an interactive region for one. The remaining controls are positioned correctly and behave normally.

