8. Final acceptance criteria

The implementation is complete only when all of the following are true:

* [ ]	CPU attacks visibly face the opponent, including after a side switch.
* [ ]	Direction-locked attacks and projectiles retain correct physics.
* [ ]	Player-controlled fighter facing remains manual.
* [ ]	Jump always displays the same upward arrow.
* [ ]	No Down arrow button exists in Joystick controls.
* [ ]	No Down arrow button exists in Classic controls.
* [ ]	No Down button exists in touch layout customization.
* [ ]	Obsolete Down button UI code and styling are removed.
* [ ]	Existing saved custom layouts remain usable.
* [ ]	Ground attack icons reflect ground attacks.
* [ ]	Air attack icons reflect air attacks.
* [ ]	Attack icons refresh on jumping and landing.
* [ ]	#0002’s airborne Attack 3 displays Blue Tornado artwork.
* [ ]	#0002’s Extra Attack displays an actual tornado.
* [ ]	Ability restrictions, cooldowns, and combat balance are unchanged.
* [ ]	No multi-touch or control-layout regressions.
* [ ]	Relevant automated tests pass.

9. Delivery expectations

Implement the changes in the existing repository, not merely as a proposal.

Keep the changes focused and consistent with the existing JavaScript architecture.

After implementation, provide:

1. A summary of changes, grouped by CPU behavior, mobile controls, and attack icons.
2. The exact files modified or deleted.
3. Confirmation of how ground/air icons are selected.
4. Confirmation that #0002’s tornado image comes from its existing projectile animation.
5. Automated test results, including any failures.
6. Any remaining limitations or manual checks that could not be completed.

Priority: Correctness, consistency, clean removal of obsolete UI code, and preservation of established gameplay behavior. Do not treat merely changing button labels or hiding controls as completing these requirements.
